%% HAND-CURATED. Race-condition surfaced per plan §11: refresh-token rotation + 30s grace window protects against concurrent refresh from two app instances.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant IdentityService

    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/auth/refresh {refreshToken, X-Request-Id}
    Gateway->>Gateway: rate-limit (sys-17) — auth_refresh — 10 per minute per parent ID
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward request
    alt auth_refresh_rate_limited
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 429 auth_refresh_rate_limited
    else invalid_refresh_token
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 401 invalid_refresh_token
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 401
    else refresh_replay_detected
        Note over IdentityService: old token reused AFTER rotation grace window — revoke session + emit suspicious event (sys-13)
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 401 invalid_refresh_token
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 401
    else success
        Note over IdentityService: rotate — issue new pair, old token enters 30s grace (still accepted) to absorb concurrent refresh
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {tokens: {accessToken, refreshToken}}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    end

    Note over ParentApp,IdentityService: timeout 3s p99 — never retry on 401 — concurrent refresh from two app instances is safe within 30s rotation grace
